From: Valerie Snyder <valsnyde@cisco.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:25:59 -0400
Subject: libclamav: Enforce OLE2 property recursion limit (#157)

OLE2 file properties may reference child properties. The file-child traversal did not increment rec_level, allowing a long acyclic chain to bypass MaxRecursion and exhaust the native stack.

Increment the recursion level for file children, matching root and directory child traversal so every recursive edge is bounded.

Reported by Nebula Security.

CLAM-3071

---
Upstream: https://github.com/Cisco-Talos/clamav/commit/53b94c5bb7c0174d01674512c56ef22c43a9fca3
CVE: CVE-2026-76417
Signed-off-by: Titouan Christophe <titouan.christophe@mind.be>
---
 libclamav/ole2_extract.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libclamav/ole2_extract.c b/libclamav/ole2_extract.c
index 49df851055..73dd23ff2b 100644
--- a/libclamav/ole2_extract.c
+++ b/libclamav/ole2_extract.c
@@ -753,7 +753,7 @@ static int ole2_walk_property_tree(ole2_header_t *hdr, const char *dir, int32_t
                     cli_dbgmsg("OLE2: filesize exceeded\n");
                 }
                 if ((int)(prop_block[idx].child) != -1) {
-                    ret = ole2_walk_property_tree(hdr, dir, prop_block[idx].child, handler, rec_level, file_count, ctx, scansize, handler_ctx);
+                    ret = ole2_walk_property_tree(hdr, dir, prop_block[idx].child, handler, rec_level + 1, file_count, ctx, scansize, handler_ctx);
                     if (ret != CL_SUCCESS) {
                         ole2_list_delete(&node_list);
                         return ret;
